# Personal Website Redesign — Implementation Plan

---

## First: The Resume Question

You asked a great question — *"I wanted the site to replace a CV, so isn't the resume-style home page the right move?"*

**Short answer:** Yes, resume-style CAN be world-class. The issue isn't the structure — it's the execution. Here's the full comparison:

### Resume-Style vs. Creative vs. Hybrid

| Aspect | Pure Resume-Style | Pure Creative | **Hybrid (Recommended)** |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Goal** | Replace PDF resume | Express personality | Replace resume AND express personality |
| **Home page** | All sections dumped in order | Abstract/artistic intro | **Curated** highlights with personality |
| **Who uses it** | Corporate/finance/tech | Designers/artists | Brittany Chiang, Lee Robinson, most successful dev portfolios |
| **Recruiter-friendly** | ✅ Easy to scan | ❌ Hard to find info | ✅ Easy to scan with better engagement |
| **Memorable** | ❌ Forgettable | ✅ Memorable | ✅ Memorable AND useful |
| **"Shows the me"** | ❌ Shows the resume | ✅ Shows the person | ✅ Shows BOTH |

### What's Wrong With Your CURRENT Resume Layout

It's not that it's resume-style — it's that it's a **data dump**, not a **curated resume**:

| Problem | Your Home Page Now | A Good Resume-Style Home Page |
|---|---|---|
| **Content volume** | Everything: experience, education, certifications, skills | Curated: hero + 2-3 featured things + key credentials |
| **Duplication** | Education appears here AND on `/education` | Education details only on `/education`, summary on home |
| **Prioritization** | Leads with "Leadership & Experience" (community orgs) | Leads with strongest signal (featured projects or key credential) |
| **Visual hierarchy** | Thin lines between text blocks | Clear visual breaks, accent colors, maybe a featured card |
| **Personality** | Zero — reads identical to any BBA student's site | Opening line, writing voice, or visual choice that's uniquely yours |

### The Hybrid Approach: Resume Structure WITH Soul

**Keep the resume structure. Fix the curation.** Here's what changes:

```
CURRENT HOME PAGE:                    PROPOSED HOME PAGE:
┌──────────────────────┐              ┌──────────────────────┐
│ Name (Hero)          │              │ Name (Hero)          │
│ LinkedIn headline    │              │ Personal philosophy  │ ← placeholder for now
│ Bio paragraph        │              │ (you write later)    │
├──────────────────────┤              ├──────────────────────┤
│ Experience (4 items) │              │ Featured Work (2-3)  │ ← your best projects
│ Education (4 items)  │              │ with screenshots     │   with actual visuals
│ Certifications       │              ├──────────────────────┤
│ Skills dots          │              │ Experience (4 items) │ ← same as now
└──────────────────────┘              ├──────────────────────┤
                                      │ Credentials          │ ← certifications + 
                                      │ (compact)            │   skills combined
                                      ├──────────────────────┤
                                      │ Latest Whisper       │ ← shows you're a thinker
                                      └──────────────────────┘
```

**What moves out:**
- Full education details → stay on `/education` page only (no duplication)

**What moves in:**
- 2-3 featured projects (with screenshot placeholders)
- Latest whisper entry

**What stays but improves:**
- Experience section → same content, same position
- Credentials → certifications + skills merged into one compact section

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This isn't "removing resume content." It's **promoting your best work** and **removing duplication** with the education page.

---

## URL Recommendation

| URL | Pros | Cons | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| `jabirah.pages.dev` | Short, clean, personal, memorable | `.pages.dev` is less recognized | **🏆 Best choice** |
| `jabirah.vercel.app` | Clean | `.vercel.app` screams "developer side project" | Runner-up |
| `jabir-a-h.github.io/personal-website/` | Shows GitHub presence | Long, has subpath, looks unfinished | Worst for sharing |

**Recommendation:** Use `jabirah.pages.dev` as primary. Set the others as redirects. All OG meta tags, sitemap, and canonical URLs should point to `jabirah.pages.dev`.

